# A .gitignore is a list of files git must leave alone.
# Anything matching a line below stays on your computer and never gets uploaded.
# Copy this file into your own projects. Read every line, there are only a few.

# Keys and passwords. This is the important part.
.env
.env.*
# The exception: a .env.example holds fake placeholder values, so it is safe to upload.
!.env.example

# Downloaded code libraries. Big, and rebuilt from scratch anyway.
node_modules/
.venv/

# Files your computer creates by itself, that nobody else needs.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Anything you want kept private. Put files in a folder with this name.
private/
